WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.690
First of all,
social media is free.

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.750
So that's the best
thing that somebody

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.715
would have going for
them is that their--

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:09.610
their own marketing team.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.940
So if you start small
and you figure out

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.420
what it is that you have to
offer and then go from there.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.920
I think it's
really important what

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.900
you say about social media being
free, because if you've got--

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.555
Oh, yeah.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.180
 --if you know your product and
you know yourself and you know

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.790
what you can offer to people,
you can put that out there

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.280
on social media and grow a
community over time that can

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.980
then support whatever it is
you're trying to sell, right?

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.360
Well, and you have your
very own focus group.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:35.860
Uh-huh.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.240
It's like a built-in focus
group of really testing ideas.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.440
You must have-- each one of us
has various things inside of us

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.700
that we have as a dream--

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:45.910
Yeah.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.702
 --or something we'd
love to do, you know?

00:00:47.702 --> 00:00:50.740
We just-- you have to really dig
deep, figure out what that is.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.990
And then if you
have a focus group,

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.360
like a social media
platform, then you

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.710
can sort of figure out
what's going to work for you.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.210
Yeah.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.210
I remember Kim on
Twitter in the early days

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.170
was choosing a color
cap for her fragrance.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:03.670
Right.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.170
Right.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.850
And she was also choosing--
asking people what she should

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.230
wear to one of the
awards ceremonies.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.280
It was something that
she taught the rest of us--

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.000
how to utilize social
media in figuring out,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.660
you know, how your
community responds to you,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:23.980
who's following you, and then
how to engage with those people

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.330
and have a relationship.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.480
And that was something that
she taught the rest of us.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.820
Is when she did
that first fragrance

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.980
and she said, "what color
should I do the bottle?"

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.480
Yeah.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.750
I was shocked how
many people responded.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.250
Yeah.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.253
And then she actually did--

00:01:38.253 --> 00:01:38.920
The one that--

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.030
 --follow what
everybody voted for.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:41.530
Right.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.720
So I thought that
was really also gaining

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.152
the trust of the people
that were following her,

00:01:46.152 --> 00:01:48.610
because they believed that she
was going to listen to them.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:54.760
Well, I have a very small,
intimate, powerful, kick ass,

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.650
just state of the art team.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.200
I'm so proud of you
guys and everything

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.370
that we built together.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:05.170
And I think that, for me, one
of the things that's been--

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:08.095
you can probably answer this
better than I, because you're--

00:02:08.095 --> 00:02:10.960
[LAUGHS] you're the leader
of the team at times.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.130
But I think that, for me,
it's trusting one another.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.330
And we have longevity together.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.038
We've been through
so much together,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.830
which a lot of people
that are starting out

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.820
don't have that yet.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.320
Right.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.210
But I think that you have
to, again, use your instincts.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.830
It's about chemistry.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.900
And I think that when
we're on the same page,

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.830
and when you're on the
same page as your partners

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.860
and your teammates,
that that's everything.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.350
Being available to people,
even though you have, like,

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:38.500
the craziest--

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.430
You have to be available.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:39.790
You have to.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.020
You have to be available.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.280
You have to be dialed in.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.420
You have to be connected.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.970
You have to know what's
going on all the time.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.250
And you have to be ready for
whatever is thrown your way.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:49.750
Yeah.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.120
I mean, every single day we--

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.285
I feel like a fireman.

00:02:53.285 --> 00:02:53.785
Yeah.

00:02:53.785 --> 00:02:54.285
You know?

00:02:54.285 --> 00:02:57.440
We're just putting out fires
left and right all the time.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.810
And I think that with
that attitude of anything

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.880
is possible, that
goes a long way.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.090
I think everybody has
self-doubt from time to time.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:13.360
I mean, I do, you know,
often think, "OK, is this--

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.960
am I doing," especially
because I'm everyone's manager

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.300
and I don't want to
disappoint anybody.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.900
And I'm a people pleaser--

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.550
I really am.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.650
As strong as I am, it's--

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.323
that soft, you know?

00:03:25.323 --> 00:03:27.490
There's another side of me
that just wants everybody

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.032
to be happy--

00:03:28.032 --> 00:03:28.570
Yeah.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.822
 --everybody to be, you
know, in control of their day,

00:03:31.822 --> 00:03:33.655
happy about the decisions
that we're making.

00:03:33.655 --> 00:03:36.190
You know, so that's
my self-doubt.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.830
It's not actually doubt, it's
just I'm a people pleaser.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.890
I think you have to
have really tough skin.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:45.250
I mean, any time you enter
the world of social media,

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.190
you're opening yourself
up for criticism.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:52.630
And it's just part of what
these platforms are subject to.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.990
And I think that you
have to stay focused

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:59.740
on what you're doing, stay
focused on what is happening,

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.931
and--

00:04:00.931 --> 00:04:03.910
and what you really want to
communicate to the people that

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:07.750
are following you, and not worry
about complete strangers that

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.730
are criticizing you
and attacking you

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.180
that have never even met you.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:11.680
Right.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.430
[MUSIC PLAYING]

